1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,766
Finish Line.

2
00:00:00,766 --> 00:00:02,872
Same checkout, six ways through.

3
00:00:02,872 --> 00:00:05,744
This demo uses computer generated narration.

4
00:00:05,744 --> 00:00:12,638
These are actual recorded browser measurements on a controlled bakery fixture, not an AI builder benchmark.

5
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:14,297
Four of six lanes finish.

6
00:00:14,297 --> 00:00:17,935
The screen reader and voice lanes stop at real barriers.

7
00:00:17,935 --> 00:00:19,276
Counts are measured.

8
00:00:19,276 --> 00:00:21,637
The human time clock is an estimate.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,597
Each lane opens its evidence.

10
00:00:33,597 --> 00:00:37,068
The screen reader lane reached a button without a usable name.

11
00:00:37,068 --> 00:00:41,474
You can inspect the actual browser frame, its announcement and the event trail.

12
00:00:41,474 --> 00:00:44,118
The fix prompt comes from a closed reason code.

13
00:00:44,118 --> 00:00:49,957
Nothing here is a human screen reader session, and a finished lane is not a certificate of accessibility.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,797
The engine has a published correctness matrix.

15
00:00:59,797 --> 00:01:02,958
Ten deliberately isolated fixtures, six lanes each.

16
00:01:02,958 --> 00:01:09,524
All sixty expectations pass, including focus traps, missing names, mismatched labels, occlusion and reflow.

17
00:01:09,524 --> 00:01:13,841
Unknown engine failures are kept separate from accessibility failures.

18
00:01:13,841 --> 00:01:17,549
The method also publishes its limits and timing assumptions.

19
00:01:18,049 --> 00:01:20,358
This is the repaired controlled bakery.

20
00:01:20,358 --> 00:01:25,864
It follows the same three step journey: add the first product, open the cart, then checkout.

21
00:01:25,864 --> 00:01:28,232
The dated rerun finishes all six lanes.

22
00:01:28,232 --> 00:01:31,725
Both versions retain their real timelines and screenshots.

23
00:01:31,725 --> 00:01:35,751
We do not attribute these hand authored fixtures to any AI builder.

24
00:01:50,049 --> 00:01:54,303
For an authorized public site, paste its URL and inspect real controls.

25
00:01:54,303 --> 00:01:56,520
Select up to three actions in order.

26
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:01,313
Preview can replay earlier selections to reveal the next page or a cart drawer.

27
00:02:01,313 --> 00:02:05,866
It requires authorization because those actions can change the target site.

28
00:02:05,866 --> 00:02:08,503
This example only inspects example dot com.

29
00:02:12,049 --> 00:02:15,487
The real Deployxa account is connected in read only mode.

30
00:02:15,487 --> 00:02:20,433
Cloud writes, purchases, rollback and AI requests are blocked by the application.

31
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:22,604
No resources have been provisioned.

32
00:02:22,604 --> 00:02:29,540
The account's reported fifty dollar usage ceiling does not guarantee zero spending, so hosting remains unverified.

33
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,409
No paid upgrade is authorized.

34
00:02:32,049 --> 00:02:34,790
Finish Line also races its own Start button.

35
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:37,718
All six lanes finish that one step self check.

36
00:02:37,718 --> 00:02:43,885
Automated accessibility checks pass, while human keyboard and screen reader checks remain pending.

37
00:02:43,885 --> 00:02:48,308
Original AI builder exports are still required for the real benchmark.

38
00:02:48,308 --> 00:02:50,613
This is the working local prototype.

39
00:02:50,613 --> 00:02:51,298
Push code.

40
00:02:51,298 --> 00:02:52,481
Everyone finishes.
